{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Return, return, O Shulamite</b><br>The Shulamite — she is from the city of Shalem, which is Jerusalem, as in \"His tabernacle is in Shalem\" (Psalms 76:3)." "As the dance of Mahanaim — with timbrel and flute." "<b>Return a second time</b><br>I would hear them saying to me, \"Return, return, O Shulamite.\" And I would answer them: \"What do you seek in the Shulamite, that you have all come out to see her — like the dance of the two camps, as when women go forth with timbrel and flute at the king's arrival?\" And this is the meaning of Machanaim." "<b>Return a third time</b><br>The Shekhinah said: Even though you rebelled and you are in exile, you shall yet return, and the entire world will marvel at you, and they shall go out to meet you with dances."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "The phrase כמחולת המחנים is repeated from the verse; Ibn Ezra first gives a terse reading (comment 1), then a fuller narrative-context reading here. The bracketed [כולכם] is a manuscript variant."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:53.136309192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}